# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/fusion-2 window (the prefill levers on the ship stack: the prefill SDPA with one q chunk per core, WPP, and the 13x10 matmul grids, M1; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/fusion-2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-6 is the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (the oneq lever needs its binary; every arm without the flag runs that binary with the lever off). A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# A1 (EXACTNESS of the combination, STOP): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-oneq-grid13-audit = the audited combined fusion arm
# (c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-audit: every integrated lever with its audit) plus QWEN_FAST_SDPA_PF_ONEQ=1 and QWEN_FAST_SDPA_PF_ONEQ_AUDIT=1 (the
# prefill SDPA with one q chunk per core, its audit running the chain's own program beside it on the same operands and comparing both outputs bit for bit on every chip)
# plus QWEN_FAST_GRID13=1 and QWEN_FAST_GRID13_AUDIT=1 (the three fused prefill all-gather matmuls on 12 columns, the verify block's output projections on 54 cores and the
# fused commit's feature projection on the device-wide grid, each audited against the served configuration on the same operands). The smoke runs the warm-up (the eager
# prefill and verify warm passes are where both audits fire), the SOLO prefill ladder (four real-code prompts of about 4,096 / 32,768 / 131,072 / 253,920 tokens, one
# request at a time: the lever in every chunk) and eight live. READ: c2_smoke_check clean under EVERY rule at once (the fusion rules of the fifteen combined levers, the
# oneq marker rule and the M1 rule grid13_smoke): '[PINDIAG] sdpa prefill oneq engaged' and '[PINDIAG] sdpa prefill oneq audit n=.. exact=True'; '[PINDIAG] tp4 grid13
# engaged' for site=gdn_in, site=attn_in, the MLP's site and site=verify.out and '[PINDIAG] tp4 grid13 audit n=.. exact=True site=..' for each; NO 'fell back' line of
# either lever, no 'audit mismatch', no stall, every answer complete. A 'lacks the oneq edits' error means the image is not B0's (the K64j binary). ANY mismatch, fallback
# or missing line is NO-GO for the combination and halts the window: bisect with references/fusion-jobs/M1/M1A (grid13 alone) and references/fusion-jobs/WPP/OQ-A1 (oneq
# alone), on this image. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through the smoke step (AICLK
# and the limiter holding it, power, current, temperature); read telemetry-smoke/telemetry-summary.txt beside the result, and the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode
# check ok. It runs on the host and is not part of any arm; it is on every leg so the pairs stay paired. A gain that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is
# the clocks, not the lever. Duration (estimate): boot 12 minutes, the audited ladder 8, the steady window 30; 70 minutes in all; the box is 100.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-6
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-oneq-grid13-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,prefill_ladder_solo,concurrent8_steady
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=100
